            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Disclosed is a data transmission method. The method comprises: a terminal device receiving first downlink control information (DCI) and second DCI scrambled based on different radio network temporary identities (RNTIs), wherein the first DCI comprises first resource allocation information for a first channel, and the first resource allocation information indicates a first resource region, and the second DCI comprises second resource allocation information for the first channel, and the second resource allocation information indicates a second resource region; and the terminal device determining that the first channel scheduled by the second DCI is transmitted in a third resource region, wherein the third resource region is a resource region obtained by removing an overlapping region of the first resource region and the second resource region from the second resource region. Further disclosed are another data transmission method, a network device, a user equipment and a storage medium.</p>
            </abstract>
